      "heading": "A — Pennsylvania Class C knowledge-test authority for Regulatory signs",
      "learner_facing": true,
      "markdown": "## A — Pennsylvania Class C knowledge-test authority for Regulatory signs\nIssuer: the cover identifies Pennsylvania Department of Transportation and its Bureau of Driver Licensing [A01].\nDocument edition: the cover carries PUB 95 (4-21) English Version [A01].\nScope: the handbook prepares applicants for a non-commercial Class C license, including ordinary passenger vehicles, pickups and vans [A02].\nThe knowledge examination contains 18 multiple-choice items [A03].\nPassing requires correct answers to 15 of the questions [A03].\nNo passing percentage is asserted because the cited sentence gives a correct-answer count (verify PA-sec04-A-PERCENT).\nNo test duration is asserted because the selected evidence provides no time limit (verify PA-sec04-A-TIME).\nThe current issuer page links this handbook, but the edition is old and no effective date is stated; changes since its publication require evidence review (verify PA-sec04-A-FRESH, PA-sec04-A-EFFECTIVE).\nPractice mastery requirements are product policy and are separate from the issuer examination standard.\n",
